0012: _SFLOAT members in the integer UBWC compat classes of fd6_ubwc_compat_mode().

Relations: standalone - edits only fd6_ubwc_compat_mode()
(src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h). Complements 0006 (other rows of
the same switch) and 0011 (other format families): three edits of one
compat table, but different parts of it, they apply together without
conflicts. The mechanism differs from 0005/0010 - those decide whether a
list stays tiled, this one decides whether UBWC turns on at all (on gen2
an incompatible list clears ubwc_enabled unconditionally).

Why. The stock code keeps every _FLOAT out of fd6_ubwc_compat_mode(), and
for R32_FLOAT it says outright «a630 blob allows these, but not a660».
a660 is our gen2 family, so the decision is deliberate, not an oversight.
But because of it, any format list in which _SFLOAT is mixed with
integers fails tu6_mutable_format_list_ubwc_compatible() and loses
compression entirely.

That is exactly how five vkd3d classes are built, i.e. precisely what
D3D12 builds for TYPELESS resources (R32_TYPELESS, R16G16_TYPELESS,
R32G32_TYPELESS, R16G16B16A16_TYPELESS, R32G32B32A32_TYPELESS). Out of 70
vkd3d classes, 31 hold UBWC on stock and the remaining 39 lose it; this
patch raises 31 -> 36.

Justification by layouts, not by the blob. UBWC encoding is defined per
format class, not per concrete format, and within one class only the
channel sizes differ. An _SFLOAT member has exactly the same layout as
the integer member of the same typeless format: same bits per channel,
same swizzle, same tiled markup. A Vulkan cast is a reinterpretation of
the same bits, not a channel permutation, so fast-clear and sector
decoding cannot diverge. Z32_FLOAT deliberately stays UNKNOWN: it belongs
to no color typeless family, and depth has its own clear semantics.

What this patch does not check (and remains a risk): the driver does not
compare the contents of the UBWC fast-clear metadata against the format
interpretation, so a wrong clear value can only show up where an
application does a fast-clear through a view with float interpretation.
A byte roundtrip does not catch this.

Measured on Adreno 740 (chip_id 0x43050a01), probe U in
tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c, over five TYPELESS classes:

  stock (0004-0006):  list=0x100000 vs nonmut=0x102000  -> list dropped UBWC
  with patch:         list=0x102000                      -> list kept it

  roundtrip (CopyBufferToImage -> CopyImageToBuffer, byte-by-byte compare):
  stock  linear/nonmut/list  0/262144, 0/262144, 0/262144    EXACT
  patch  linear/nonmut/list  0/262144, 0/262144, 0/262144    EXACT

Isolated A/B on the 0005-0010 stack (04.10.2026): the presence of the
patch changes exactly 5 lines of probe U, everything else is identical
(results/test-stack.log vs results/test-0012.log). The driver backup log
from 02.10 (results/test-backup-oct2.log) matches byte for byte the run
of stack+this patch - the backup was built with it.

No regressions: probes S (0005) and T (0006) are still PASS.

Promoted from experiments/0008-experiment-sfloat-int-ubwc-compat.patch
(04.10.2026). The fast-clear caveat is kept; analysis - docs/analysis.md,
section 20.5.

